var e=`# CHAPTER 4 — Jasmine

Inside, things got way too good.

Big Kim slid across the floor with his smoothest moves, nice and slow, all the way to his target: the buffet table. And he stood guard. Nothing in this life could pull Big Kim away from there. Not one waiter got past him without him grabbing two glasses, and that's where he used his most incredible skill: both hands serving himself at the same time.

Me, on the other hand, I'm hungry for something else at this kind of event.

Unfortunately I fly solo. Kim is not what you'd call a *wingman*. And good thing he isn't, because he ruins my game more than he helps.

---

I started strutting around. A little drink here, a little chat there. The kids from school gave me some crooked little smiles, but the outside crowd was chill. I saw some drugs going around too. Rich-kid party: everybody underage, everybody relaxed.

Every now and then I'd swing by to check on my boy. Still there. Eating everything, drinking everything.

And me making my rounds. A cutie here, a hug there.

---

Then I spotted an interesting target.

They all were, but this one had something. Brown skin, just the way I like it. Wavy honey-colored hair falling over her face. And a little wickedness in her eyes.

I moved in slow, introduced myself, made some conversation. In no time she was laughing and I was stroking her pretty face. She's the one who came closer.

Things heated up. In a house that size, there was definitely a room available. She liked the idea.

We went up the stairs holding hands.

From there on, my friend, it's between the couple. Stays between us.

---

About an hour later, she said she was satisfied and wanted to go back down. I let her go, obviously. I don't own anybody. We each went off to enjoy the party our own way.

I went downstairs, checked on Kim. All good.

And then, out of nowhere, there was screaming. The music stopped.

Up top there was a blond guy losing his mind.
`;export{e as default};
